Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "NighttimeUrbanDriving" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :description "Multiple vehicles stationary or moving slowly in a nighttime urban setting with potential lane intrusion" ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 .

:weather1 a :NightCondition .

:actor1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Red vehicle in right lane" .
:actor2 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Green vehicle in right lane" .
:actor3 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "White vehicle in right lane" .
:actor4 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Black vehicle in left lane" .

:risk1 a :LaneIntrusionRisk ;
    :description "Vehicles in right lane moving slowly, potentially intruding into left lane" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :RearEndCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Slow-moving vehicles may cause rear-end collision" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Buildings and parked vehicles may occlude visibility of oncoming traffic" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.65"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.55"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

**Risk 1:**
Description: Vehicles in the right lane moving slowly, potentially intruding into the left lane.
Severity Score: 0.75

**Risk 2:**
Description: Slow-moving vehicles may cause a rear-end collision.
Severity Score: 0.65

**Risk 3:**
Description: Buildings and parked vehicles may occlude visibility of oncoming traffic.
Severity Score: 0.55

---
The scene was classified as a **StateAnomaly** due to the unusual state of vehicles moving slowly or being stationary in a nighttime urban setting, which deviates from typical driving behavior and poses risks. The identified risks are based on the observed conditions and potential hazards in the scene.